Round runner change (after round 18g): a crashed sitting is not the painter's judgment.

Round 18g's GEM lane (gemini-3.8-flash) hit Google's 2M input tokens/min: sitting 1 exited 1
on the 429 after painting 23 chunks, sitting 2 exited 1 on the next 429 after 9 s, and the
runner took sitting 2's "no new painting chunks" for the painter being done. With this patch a
sitting that exits non-zero, or whose pi session ends on a provider error (stopReason
"error"), is a crash: the runner waits (90, 180, 300, 600, 900, 1200 s, or the provider's
"retry in Ns" + 15 s if longer) and starts another sitting that doesn't count toward
MAX_SITTINGS; after MAX_CRASHES (6) crashes it stops the painter and logs STOPPED. Only a
clean sitting with no new painting chunks ends the painter. Sittings are numbered in order,
retakes included (files p1_s<k>_*.txt never overwritten); records an older runner marked
"completed" with a non-zero exit are reclassified as crashes on resume. Also: model(...,
env={...}) passes per-lane environment to the painter's pi (harness/painter reads
PAINTER_MAX_IMAGES, PAINTER_MAX_IMAGE_MB, PAINTER_INPUT_TPM; r17-base 76eccdf).

Written against r18/r18_open.py (and its test_painting_chunks.py); applied as is to
r18g/r18g_open.py. Not applied to any running runner. Apply to a copy of the next runner:
    cd <new round dir> && patch -p1 < ~/tmp/gallery-fcf9c110/r17/next_round_2.patch
(for a runner with another name, rename the file in the patch headers first).

